    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "How is digital marketing for logistics companies different from generic B2B marketing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Logistics buyers do not behave like SaaS buyers. A shipper choosing a 3PL, a D2C brand choosing a courier, or an importer choosing a freight forwarder makes decisions based on network coverage, service-level guarantees, price + fuel-surcharge transparency, tech + tracking capability, and industry-specific compliance (cold-chain, hazmat, cross-border). Digital marketing that ignores this reads like brochure content and fails to convert. At ITD GrowthLabs we build category-specific funnels around real logistics decision moments — RFP season, warehouse expansion, peak-season capacity contracts, cold-chain compliance renewals — with content, ads and landing pages designed for those specific triggers."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Who is this service for at ITD GrowthLabs?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "3PL and 4PL operators, courier + last-mile delivery companies, freight forwarders (air + ocean + road), cold-chain / temperature-controlled logistics, international couriers, e-commerce fulfilment providers, warehousing operators, hyperlocal delivery businesses, cross-border customs / clearance houses, and supply-chain SaaS + tech businesses. Typical revenue band is Rs 5 Cr-500 Cr for founder-led companies, plus large-enterprise marketing teams inside publicly listed logistics groups."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What makes ITD GrowthLabs specifically qualified for logistics companies vs a generic agency?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Three things. First, we already build the software logistics companies run on — Courier Management Software, Logistics Mobile App, and 5 delivered SaaS engagements (Courier Management System, Cross-Border Courier Platform, Fleet Management for 3PL, On-Demand Courier Booking, Smart Logistics SaaS Platform). Second, our founder built Trackmate Lite, a logistics SaaS in production use, so category vocabulary is native — we understand OSMs, DTOs, AWB flow, POD, cash-on-delivery reconciliation, hub-and-spoke vs point-to-point routing, and how each shapes marketing narratives. Third, we have a live client (CourierDost) whose engagement covers marketing + product both, so we know how buyers actually shop for these services."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which digital marketing channels work best for logistics companies?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It depends on who buys. For B2B freight and 3PL, LinkedIn ABM + Google Search Ads (high-intent phrases like 'freight forwarder Mumbai to Dubai' or '3PL warehousing Bhiwandi') + long-form SEO content + industry PR work best. For D2C-facing couriers and last-mile ops, Meta Ads targeting Shopify + WooCommerce merchants + Google Ads on courier-service terms + WhatsApp broadcast funnels work best. For cross-border / international shipping, LinkedIn Sales Nav ABM + gated whitepapers + industry-event follow-up + email nurture win. We tailor the mix — most clients run a 40% SEO / 35% paid / 15% content / 10% WhatsApp+LinkedIn ABM split, adjusted by segment."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is a realistic budget to start with?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Our Starter Growth Retainer begins at Rs 65,000 per month and covers SEO foundation, one paid channel (usually Google Ads or Meta Ads), 4 monthly blog articles and a monthly review call. Rs 1.5 lakh per month unlocks the Growth Retainer — 3 paid channels, LinkedIn ABM, WhatsApp funnel, weekly reporting, and campaign landing pages. Rs 4 lakh+ per month unlocks Enterprise / Multi-Region — full-stack marketing including PR, video, case-study production and India + GCC + international expansion. Ad spend is on top of retainer, typically Rs 50,000-Rs 10 lakh per month for smaller ops and Rs 5 lakh-Rs 50 lakh+ for larger 3PL and freight companies."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long before we see leads?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "SEO + content shows measurable movement in 90-120 days and compounds from month 4-6 onwards. Paid channels (Google Ads + Meta + LinkedIn) generate qualified leads from week 2, but the first 3-4 weeks are optimisation. WhatsApp broadcast funnels can start converting nurture-list buyers in the first campaign. We set 30-day, 90-day and 180-day milestones during onboarding so timelines are contractual, not aspirational."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can you handle international shipping / freight forwarding marketing across India, GCC and USA?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. We already run India + GCC dual-market campaigns for several clients across e-commerce, real estate and D2C. For logistics we can support English + Hindi + Arabic creative production, INR + AED + USD pricing narratives, and market-specific compliance messaging (GDPR + India DPDP + UAE data localisation). Our GCC city presence covers Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, Jebel Ali, Riyadh, Jeddah and Dammam."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you build our website + landing pages too, or only run campaigns?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Both. Website is a required foundation — most logistics companies lose 30-60% of qualified traffic on generic websites with weak trust signals, unclear service scope and slow load. We rebuild logistics websites for conversion (quote-request forms, live tracking widget, coverage-map interactives, service-area SEO, service-level SLA callouts) and run all paid + organic on top. We can also build custom logistics software (courier management, TMS, fleet apps) via our engineering team."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What kind of content works for logistics companies?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Real, first-hand, buyer-question content. Not '10 tips for logistics companies'. Best-performing topics: rate comparison guides ('Mumbai to Bengaluru courier cost 2026'), service comparison ('DHL vs Blue Dart vs Delhivery for cross-border'), 3PL selection guides for D2C founders, RFP templates for procurement teams, cold-chain compliance checklists, and city-level logistics guides. We produce all of this in-house with editors who have logistics-industry familiarity — not generic content mills."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do we start?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Two options. Book a free 30-minute discovery call via our Calendly and we will map your growth funnel + share a customised proposal within 3 working days. Or WhatsApp us at +91-9930950940 with your website URL and current monthly ad spend and we will send back a 1-page audit within 24 hours. No pushy sales — we walk away from engagements that are not a fit."}}]}</script>
